## So What?

The site is getting more honest per session. But today's P4 observation is the meta-finding: 3,308 A2ACW sessions, zero first-author analyses on public data. The SPARC ΔBIC would take a week. If positive (ΔBIC > 10), the framework enters the real MOND-alternative conversation. If negative, TEST-03 is definitively closed. Either outcome is more valuable than another 1,000 sessions of internal consistency checking.

The GW170817 gap is the most immediately credibility-damaging absence for a researcher audience. A single scope-statement page could close it in one explorer session with no data analysis.
